From 1508429f6d9f3d1757a41c23a813286eb2b84d3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:48:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] can: isotp: ignore CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA without
 CAN_ISOTP_RX_PADDING

CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA checks the padding bytes of received frames
against the rxpad_content, which is only defined together with
CAN_ISOTP_RX_PADDING. iso15765-2.rst documents that CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA
is ignored when CAN_ISOTP_RX_PADDING is not specified.

Together with CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_LEN the flag is ignored as documented and
only the optimized frame length is checked. But when
CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA is set without CAN_ISOTP_RX_PADDING and without
CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_LEN, check_pad() does not ignore the flag but rejects
every received frame: SFs and the last CF of a PDU are dropped with
EBADMSG and every FC aborts the transmission with EBADMSG.

Ignore CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA without CAN_ISOTP_RX_PADDING in this case
as well, as documented. This only affects a misconfiguration that has
never been able to receive any PDU. Therefore the patch has no Fixes tag.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 net/can/isotp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/can/isotp.c b/net/can/isotp.c
index 22bfc1c..b237b1f 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp.c
@@ -426,8 +426,8 @@ static int check_pad(struct isotp_sock *so, struct canfd_frame *cf,
 		if (so->opt.flags & CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_LEN)
 			return check_optimized(cf, start_index);
 
-		/* no valid test against empty value => ignore frame */
-		return 1;
+		/* no rx padding content => ignore CAN_ISOTP_CHK_PAD_DATA */
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	/* check datalength of correctly padded CAN frame */
